In the above schema, we have defined the text2vec-openai and generative-openai modules.

The text2vec-openai module is used to vectorize the content field, while the generative-openai

module is used to generate the response. We will store the role of the message (either “user” or

“assistant”) in the role field, the content of the message in the content field, and the index of the

message in the index field (the counter).

OpenAI GPT is responsible for generating both the user and the assistant responses.

The end-user will not see that the messages are coming from “user” or “assistant” since we are going

to define two characters completely different from the user and the assistant. We are also going to

define two different personalities for the user and the assistant. Everything is defined in the prompt.

